{"created": "2026-07-12T06:46:57.817057+00:00", "modified": "2026-07-12T06:46:58.461568+00:00", "id": 21318697, "conceptrecid": "21318696", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21318697", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21318696", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21318697", "metadata": {"title": "Preliminary Summary of Harmonic Readout and c=1 Area Sweep in an AB Two-Body Closed Phase System", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21318697", "publication_date": "2026-07-12", "description": "This release publishes a preliminary summary of six AB two-body closed phase system experiments. The experiments show that acceleration-like harmonic readout can be constructed from the label-free two-body relation f_AB without introducing external standard forces, individual forces f_A/f_B, or a background space. They also show that the AB two-body system alone lacks an independent gauge for deciding whether the acceleration-like readout follows proportional, inverse, or inverse-square dependence on position phase difference. Internal c=1 calibration and chi-tau area readout can be established, but native inverse-area scaling was not detected.", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Kihara, Noriaki", "affiliation": "WF System Co., Ltd.", "orcid": "0009-0004-6753-4020"}], "keywords": ["AB two-body closed phase system", "harmonic readout", "acceleration-like readout", "label-free relation", "c=1 internal calibration", "chi-tau area", "inverse-area diagnosis", "native readout", "wave information readout"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21315735", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}, {"identifier": "10.5281/zenodo.21308049", "relation": "isSupplementTo", "resource_type": "publication-preprint", "scheme": "doi"}], "version": "v1", "language": "eng", "resource_type": {"title": "Preprint", "type": "publication", "subtype": "preprint"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21318696"}}]}, "notes": "This paper does not claim a derivation of standard gravity or a native inverse-square law. Its scope is the AB two-body closed phase system: acceleration-like harmonic readout is constructible, while distance-exponent readout remains indeterminate without an independent gauge."}, "title": "Preliminary Summary of Harmonic Readout and c=1 Area Sweep in an AB Two-Body Closed Phase System", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21318697", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21318697", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21318697?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21318697", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21318697", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21318697", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21318697/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21318696", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/21318696", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21318696", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.21318696", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21318697/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21318697/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21318697/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/21318697/media-files", "thumbnails": {"10": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21318697:ab_two_body_harmonic_readout_c1_area_sweep_preliminary_summary_ja.pdf/full/%5E10,/0/default.jpg", "50": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21318697:ab_two_body_harmonic_readout_c1_area_sweep_preliminary_summary_ja.pdf/full/%5E50,/0/default.jpg", "100": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21318697:ab_two_body_harmonic_readout_c1_area_sweep_preliminary_summary_ja.pdf/full/%5E100,/0/default.jpg", "250": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:21318697:ab_two_body_harmonic_readout_c1_area_sweep_preliminary_summary_ja.pdf/full